und colour C.\n- From each of the box's four corners, a diagonal line of 4s runs outward to the grid edge, so the box looks like the centre of a big X.\n\n**Where the box goes.** I compared the box's old and new positions with the path endpoints:\n\n| pair | C-cell | 4-cell | displacement | box top-left → new top-left |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | (1,14) | (4,15) | (+3,+1) | (7,4) → (10,5) |\n| 2 | (25,7) | (28,10) | (+3,+3) | (12,15) → (15,18) |\n| 3 | (19,24) | (24,24) | (+5,0) | (11,10) → (16,10) |\n\nIn every pair, the box moves by exactly the vector from the C endpoint to the 4 endpoint. The path works like an arrow: it goes from the colour-C end to the colour-4 end. The diagonals also match the fact sheet. For example, pair 1 has a line from (0,17) down-left to (10,7), which is the top-right corner of the moved box. Lines leave every corner, going outward (up-left, up-right, down-left, down-right).\n\n**Finding the parts in code.**\n- The box is the largest connected component of colour 4, and its centre cell gives C.\n- The arrow's C endpoint is the C-coloured cell that is not the box centre.\n- The arrow's 4 endpoint is the 4-coloured cell outside the box.\n\n**Applying it to the tests.**\n- **Test 1:** C = 1. The arrow starts at (2,2) and ends at (7,6), a displacement of (+5,+4). The box moves from (1,5) to (6,9), so it occupies rows 6–8 and columns 9–11. The background becomes 1, and diagonals run from all four corners.\n- **Test 2:** C = 6. The arrow's 6 end is at (21,17) and its 4 end is at (19,14), a displacement of (−2,−3). The box moves from (9,6) to (7,3). The background becomes 6, and diagonals run from all four corners.\n\n**Teaching stages emitted.**\n1. Fill the canvas with C.\n2. Stamp the moved ring of 4s.\n3. Draw the four diagonal rays.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    # the box: largest connected component of colour 4\n    comps = components(g == 4)\n    box = max(comps, key=len)\n    y0, x0, y1, x1 = bbox(box)\n    cy, cx = (y0 + y1) // 2, (x0 + x1) // 2\n    C = int(g[cy, cx])\n    boxset = set(box)\n    # arrow endpoints: C cell that is not the box centre, 4 cell outside the box\n    start = [(y, x) for y, x in zip(*np.where(g == C)) if (y, x) != (cy, cx)][0]\n    end = [(y, x) for y, x in zip(*np.where(g == 4)) if (y, x) not in boxset][0]\n    dy, dx = int(end[0] - start[0]), int(end[1] - start[1])\n\n    out = np.full((H, W), C, dtype=int)\n    emit(out, f\"Background becomes the box's centre colour {C}; the arrow of 5s is erased.\")\n\n    ny0, nx0, ny1, nx1 = y0 + dy, x0 + dx, y1 + dy, x1 + dx\n    for y in range(ny0, ny1 + 1):\n        for x in range(nx0, nx1 + 1):\n            if 0 <= y < H and 0 <= x < W and (y in (ny0, ny1) or x in (nx0, nx1)):\n                out[y, x] = 4\n    emit(out, f\"Box ring of 4 moved by the arrow vector ({dy},{dx}); its centre is now background.\")\n\n    corners = [(ny0, nx0, -1, -1), (ny0, nx1, -1, 1), (ny1, nx0, 1, -1), (ny1, nx1, 1, 1)]\n    for y, x, sy, sx in corners:\n        y, x = y + sy, x + sx\n        while 0 <= y < H and 0 <= x < W:\n            out[y, x] = 4\n            y += sy\n            x += sx\n    emit(out, \"Diagonal rays of 4 drawn from each box corner out to the grid edge.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"objects":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- The box is the largest connected component of colour 4, and its centre cell gives C."}],"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- The box is the largest connected component of colour 4, and its centre cell gives C."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Stamp the moved ring of 4s."}],"paths":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"A **path of 5s**."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"One end of the path touches a single cell of colour **C**, and the other end touches a single **4** cell."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- The whole background becomes C, and the 5-path and its two endpoint cells disappear."}],"rays":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Draw the four diagonal rays."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Diagonal rays of 4 drawn from each box corner out to the grid edge."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"168384f98175b1c0d8f23fca71be4e8d07e1b00f414de6dd1e870b0c24a03f40","task_sha256":"502c0d173decf510fe02e790a18a7ef223ad78bf3ce2f928708fedde8400a6e1","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
